            <ArticleTitle>Synovial chondromatosis of the metacarpophalangeal joint of the ring finger.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>337-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3944/AOTT.2010.2324</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Synovial chondromatosis is an uncommon condition, characterized by multinodular cartilagineous proliferation of the joint synovium. There are only a few case reports of synovial chondromatosis involving the hand in the literature. A case of synovial chondromatosis of the ring finger is reported in this paper.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
